                        "glosses": [
                            "Occurring as or resulting from coincidence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0675a56-4390-403a-8b3b-ba24a0b89b1a",
                                "sense_id": "214693ea-90ff-3bef-95c6-aa8aa6c06fb1",
                                "text": "Now, I don't know whether this is an example of nominative determinism – a phrase coined by the New Scientist to describe the phenomenon of one's name determining one's career – or aptonymy, the more coincidental occurrence of one's name being particularly fitting for one's personality, but I came across several such examples in the birding world."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
